{"kind":"assert","text":"Scope for the notes paths head (your c229fd58), measured on main d902e140. docs/ has no /Users/ path. notes/ has 704 files with about 4,530 matching lines. The prefixes are: artroom-evidence 4301; the shared checkout and its worktrees 292; artroom-diagnostics 82; ~/tmp/artroom-rehearsal-1 19; artroom-private-evidence 16; ~/.npm/_npx 15; artroom-worktrees 13; ~/.pyenv 6; artroom-releases 4; sibling checkouts (dap-ui-sdk, dap-foldkit, dap) 7; and the Mac mini user's home, about 35.\n\nThe rewrite I propose, mechanical and in one commit:\n1. /Users/hughpyle/play/\u003cdir\u003e/… becomes \u003cdir\u003e/… for artroom-evidence, artroom-private-evidence, artroom-diagnostics, artroom-releases, artroom-worktrees and the sibling checkouts.\n2. /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom/\u003cpath\u003e becomes the repository-relative \u003cpath\u003e (so .builder-worktrees/\u003cname\u003e); the bare checkout path becomes \"the shared checkout\".\n3. Any other /Users/hughpyle/\u003cpath\u003e becomes ~/\u003cpath\u003e.\n4. /Users/inguz/\u003cpath\u003e becomes ~inguz/\u003cpath\u003e (the Mac mini home).\n5. The check is `git grep -n \"/Users/\" -- notes` finding no line.\nEvidence citations keep their directory and file names, so they still resolve against the evidence folders.\n\nTwo questions:\n- Is this mapping right, especially rules 3 and 4? The alternative for rule 4 is \u003cmini home\u003e/\u003cpath\u003e, which also drops the user name.\n- Timing: you wrote \"after U4\". Do you mean after U4-B's witness, or may I build it now while UW-S is in review? It touches only notes/ and does not conflict with UW-S. Its 704 files put the artifact filing near the slow end.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}